          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            (a category with
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
            %em internal ring
            or a
            %em ring object
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
            to the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            of the notion of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
          %p
            Under some reasonable assumptions on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that allow one to construct a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"}> symmetric
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+objects"} group objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab(C)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
            internal to that monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab(C)
          %p
            Sometimes one might take this last point of view a little further, especially in certain contexts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            where a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            is already something like an
            = succeed "-analogue" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+abelian+groups"} category of abelian groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric smash product of spectra
            plays a role analogous to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products+of+abelian+groups"} tensor products of abelian groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            are often referred to as “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi xyz
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} xyz
            \-rings” of one sort or another (as mentioned at “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+operad"}> ring operad
            ”). Thus we have carry-over phrases from the early days of stable homotopy theory, such as “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+rings"}> A-∞ rings
            ” (for monoids) and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"}> E-∞ rings
            ” (commutative monoids). Here it is understood that the monoid multiplication on spectra is an
            = succeed "-refinement" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty, 1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            providing archetypal examples.
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %h3#traditional_definition Traditional definition
          %p
            The traditional definition, based on a traditional presentation of the
            %span.newWikiWord
              equational theory
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/equational+theory"} ?
            of rings, is that a ring object consists of an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            together with morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo ×
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a: R \times R \to R
            (addition),
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo ×
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m: R \times R \to R
            (multiplication),
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0: 1 \to R
            (zero),
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e: 1 \to R
            (multiplicative identity),
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -: R \to R
            (additive inversion), subject to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+diagrams"} commutative diagrams
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that express the usual ring axioms.
          %h3#AsAModelOfALawvereTheory As a model of a Lawvere theory
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            for rings, viz. the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
            to the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+object"} finitely generated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
            rings (which are non-commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+rings"} polynomial rings
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}\langle X_1, \ldots, X_n\rangle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a category with finite products, a
            %em ring object
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            may be identified with a product-preserving functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \to C
          %h3#ViaTheMicrocosmPrinciple Via the microcosm principle
          %p
            Alternatively, one may define ring objects following the Baez–Dolan
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microcosm+principle"} microcosm principle
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Cat
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ×
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi pt
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathsf{Cat},\times,\mathsf{pt})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoidal+category"} bimonoidal category
            (a pseudomonoid in
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi SymMonCats
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝔽
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathsf{SymMonCats},\otimes_{\mathbb{F}},\mathbb{F})
          %p
            Namely, a
            %strong
              rig in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoidal+category"} bimonoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 0
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C},\otimes_{\mathcal{C}},\oplus_{\mathcal{C}},\mathbf{0}_{\mathcal{C}},\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{C}})
            is given by a quintuple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi μ
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi η
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi μ
                    %mi R
                    %mo ×
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi η
                    %mi R
                    %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,\mu^{+}_{R},\eta^{+}_{R},\mu^{\times}_{R},\eta^{\times}_{R})
            consisting of
          %ul
            %li
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %strong underlying object
              of the rig;
            %li
              A morphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi μ
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi R
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^{+}_{R}\colon R\oplus_{\mathcal{C}}R\longrightarrow R
              %p
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong
                    addition morphism of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %li
              A morphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi μ
                        %mi R
                        %mo ×
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi R
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^{\times}_{R}\colon R\otimes_{\mathcal{C}}R\longrightarrow R
              %p
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong
                    multiplication morphism of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %li
              A morphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi η
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 0
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^{+}_{R}\colon\mathbf{0}_{\mathcal{C}}\longrightarrow R
              %p
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong
                    additive unit morphism of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %li
              A morphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi η
                        %mi R
                        %mo ×
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 1
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^{\times}_{R}\colon\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{C}}\longrightarrow R
              %p
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong
                    multiplicative unit morphism of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p satisfying the following conditions:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The triple
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi μ
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi η
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,\mu^{+}_R,\eta^{+}_R)
                is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid+in+a+symmetric+monoidal+category"}
                    commutative monoid in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %li
              %p
                The triple
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi μ
                        %mi R
                        %mo ×
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi η
                        %mi R
                        %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,\mu^{\times}_R,\eta^{\times}_R)
                is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+in+a+monoidal+category"}
                    monoid in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %li
              %p The diagrams
              %p
                %img{:src => "/nlab/files/semiring_in_bimonoidal_bilinearity_1.png", :width => "800px"}/
              %p
                corresponding to the rig axioms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                      %mi a
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a(b+c)=a b+a c
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                      %mi c
                      %mo +
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a+b)c=a c+b c
                commute;
            %li
              %p The diagrams
              %p
                %img{:src => "/nlab/files/semiring_in_bimonoidal_bilinearity_2_corr.png", :width => "500px"}/
              %p
                corresponding to the rig axioms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0a=0
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a0=0
                commute;
          %p
            Moreover, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            a
            %em braided
            bimonoidal category, one defines a
            %strong
              commutative rig in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            to be a rig in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            whose multiplicative monoid structure is commutative.
          %p
            A partial version of this definition first appeared in (
            %a{:href => "#Brun2006"}> Brun 2006, Definition 5.1
            ).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A ring object in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+ring"} topological ring
            %li
              %p
                A ring object in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28Top%29"} Ho(Top)
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-ring"} H-ring
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                equipped with a ring object is called a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+topos"} ringed topos
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+line"} affine line
                (see there) is a ring object in the given ambient
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
          %p
            For the notion of a rig in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoidal+category"} bimonoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ViaTheMicrocosmPrinciple"} defined via the microcosm principle
          %ul
            %li
              A rig in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi Sets
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ×
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ×
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\mathsf{Sets},\coprod,\times,\emptyset,\times\right)
              is a monoid.
            %li
              A rig in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi CMon
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ℕ
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\mathsf{CMon},\oplus,\otimes_\mathbb{N},0,\mathbb{N}\right)
              is a rig.
            %li
              A rig in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi Ab
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ℤ
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\mathsf{Ab},  \oplus,\otimes_\mathbb{Z},0,\mathbb{Z}\right)
              is a ring.
            %li
              A rig in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                          %mi Mod
                        %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\mathsf{Mod}_R,\oplus,\otimes_R,0,R\right)
              is an associative algebra.
            %li
              A rig in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi Cats
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ×
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ∅
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                          %mi cat
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi pt
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\mathsf{Cats},\coprod,\times,\emptyset_{\mathsf{cat}},\mathsf{pt}\right)
              is a strict monoidal category.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"}> monoid
